# Dogfood pack: the SQL-injection sinks of the real ReportService provider.
#
# The claim proved over `ReportService.Provider.SqlReportProvider.FetchRrnsAsync` is
# "no caller-supplied or ambient value reaches a SqlCommand's text". The safety
# consequence of "every SqlCommand argument is a constant or a parameter bind" is the
# same no-flow claim; the positive "is a constant or a bind" predicate is not in the
# proposition language (see wiz-notes/scry-prover-dogfood.md).
rule sql-injection
  kind taint
  severity error
  message Attacker-controlled data reaches a SQL command text
  source System.Console.ReadLine result
  source System.Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable result
  source Microsoft.AspNetCore.Http.HttpRequest.get_Headers result
  source Microsoft.AspNetCore.Http.HttpRequest.get_Query result
  sink Microsoft.Data.SqlClient.SqlCommand..ctor arg 0
  sink Microsoft.Data.SqlClient.SqlCommand.set_CommandText arg 1
  sink Microsoft.Data.SqlClient.SqlCommand.ExecuteReader arg 0
  sink Microsoft.Data.SqlClient.SqlCommand.ExecuteNonQuery arg 0
  sink Microsoft.Data.SqlClient.SqlCommand.ExecuteScalar arg 0
  sink System.Data.SqlClient.SqlCommand..ctor arg 0
  sink System.Data.SqlClient.SqlCommand.set_CommandText arg 1
end
